menu "Research CSI receiver"

config RESEARCH_RX_ESPNOW_MODE
    bool "Use the external research ESP-NOW transmitter"
    default n
    help
        Keep the CSI source-MAC filter on 1a:00:00:00:00:00 and do not start
        the receiver's legacy router-ping/null-data traffic generator. Disable
        this option to retain the legacy router-triggered CSI workflow.

config RESEARCH_RX_NULL_DATA_MODE
    bool "Use high-rate null-data CSI trigger for connected APs"
    default n
    depends on !RESEARCH_RX_ESPNOW_MODE
    help
        Send an 802.11 null-data frame every configured CSI interval after the
        station connects. The access point ACKs the frame, creating a
        high-rate CSI source for normal routers and the optional ESP32 SoftAP.
        ESP-NOW mode disables this setting and retains its dedicated workflow.

endmenu
